WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.540
The internet's boyfriend might be speeding
into one of the biggest movie franchises out

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:05.360
there.

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.680
In a recent interview with Screen Rant, long-time
Fast &amp; Furious scribe Chris Morgan revealed

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.909
that he has spoken with Keanu Reeves about
joining the film series in an upcoming entry

00:00:14.909 --> 00:00:20.120
- presumably Fast &amp; Furious 9, which Morgan
is co-writing with Daniel Casey.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.300
Morgan teased:

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.800
"I sat down with him and we're talking about
[it].

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:28.220
I wanted him to be in the Fast universe for
a very long time…The hardest thing is always

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:32.200
time and competing schedules and then designing
the right thing together.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.780
My fervent desire is to bring him into this
franchise for sure."

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:40.020
Morgan has indeed been hoping to make Reeves
an official member of the Fast family for

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:44.500
quite some time, and even got close to making
that dream a reality fairly recently.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.120
In August 2019, Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson
said that Reeves could have been in Hobbs

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:53.780
&amp; Shaw, the Fast &amp; Furious spin-off centered
on Johnson's character Luke Hobbs and his

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:57.040
onscreen frenemy Deckard Shaw, played by Jason
Statham.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:01.580
The actor told Screen Rant that the original
plan was to have Reeves portray the director

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:06.480
of the terrorist organization Eteon in Hobbs
&amp; Shaw, written by, you guessed it, Chris

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:07.360
Morgan.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:12.500
As Johnson explained, things just didn't work
out, and so the Hobbs &amp; Shaw team decided

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:17.540
to keep the identity of Eteon's director a
mystery by only revealing his voice.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:18.540
Johnson dished:

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.960
"We left the ominous voice faceless.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.700
So, for some time, I think you guys have heard
the rumor that it was going to be a bit of

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.440
a John Wick, all disguised.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:29.040
But then we left it there [with] a few people
in mind.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.000
Originally, Keanu was the goal.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.120
We were talking, and it just didn't feel right
creatively.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.240
He and I talked, and I totally got it.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.280
And it wound up being the best thing, so now
we leave that open for the future."

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:45.759
Hobbs &amp; Shaw director David Leitch also addressed
the situation in an August 2019 interview

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.060
with The Hollywood Reporter.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:51.900
The filmmaker explained that the team, quote,
"talked to Keanu early on," and that he, quote,

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:55.990
"had been talking to Keanu periodically through
the shooting of it all" and was trying to

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:58.860
decide how best to include him in Hobbs &amp; Shaw.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:03.080
In the end, though, Hobbs &amp; Shaw just wasn't
the right film to introduce Reeves into the

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:04.620
Fast &amp; Furious franchise.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:05.720
"Are you ready?"

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.540
"Yeah, I'm ready."

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:08.060
"On my three."

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:08.560
"Okay."

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:09.440
"One…"

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:10.440
"AHHH!

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.020
YOU..."

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.180
Leitch explained:

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:16.440
"I also wanted to make sure that it was enough,
a real promise for something legitimate in

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.220
the future, and wasn't just a stunt casting
role.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:23.420
We started to populate the movie with all
these other personalities, and I just didn't

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.020
really think that we needed it, although I
would've loved it.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:29.360
We even talked in post, and I showed him a
rough cut of the movie.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.480
Then, we had conversations about 'is there
something here?'

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:35.220
We came to the conclusion of 'let's put a
pin in it.'

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:39.260
I'm all for finding opportunities, but I also
didn't want to force anything."

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:43.560
The remarks from both Johnson and Leitch,
plus the revelation from Morgan about having

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:48.700
had a chat with the actor, make it seem like
Reeves could appear in Fast &amp; Furious 9 as

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:49.540
Eteon's Director.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:52.240
But is that really how he'll fit into the
Fast family?

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:55.820
Anything's possible, of course, though it's
worth questioning whether that particular

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.810
role will ever be right for Reeves.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.040
If it wasn't back then, how would it be now?

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.920
If Reeves truly will join Fast &amp; Furious 9
and he won't portray Eteon's Director in the

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:09.880
film, the best bet for the type of character
he'll embody is an antihero similar to John

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:14.980
Wick, the hired gun Reeves plays in the Derek
Kolstad-created action-thriller franchise.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:18.760
"Oh, and remember: You owe me."

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.120
"You don't want me owing you."

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:26.820
The Fast franchise has plenty of protagonists
- the most prominent of which is now Vin Diesel's

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:30.760
Dominic Toretto, and has featured a ton of
down-and-dirty villains.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:34.900
But history has shown that the characters
who aren't entirely good or completely bad

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:39.500
are some of the more interesting inclusions
in the franchise, so it's possible that Morgan,

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:44.700
Casey, and Fast 9 director Justin Lin might
want to have Reeves play a morally gray character.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:49.360
Considering the Fast &amp; Furious franchise team
has long been eyeing Reeves to join in some

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:53.780
capacity, it doesn't seem outrageous to say
they'd want to place him in a role that is

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:57.720
not only interesting and well-rounded but
that also has true staying power.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:02.520
Like Leitch said, Reeves' potential role in
the film series should have promise and legitimacy

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:05.730
so that he can continue being a part of the
movies in the future.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:10.211
Taking everything into account, it appears
that Fast &amp; Furious 9 just might be the movie

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:12.580
in which Reeves makes his franchise debut.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:17.480
And regardless of who he may play in the flick,
his appearance should be, to quote the man

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.360
himself, pretty darn breathtaking.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:22.540
"You're breathtaking!"

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:27.460
Fast &amp; Furious 9 will speed into theaters
on May 22, 2020.

